  "grammar_points": [
    {
      "name": "〜ても (te mo) — even if / even though",
      "jlpt_reference": "JLPT N4",
      "explanation": {
        "en": "How it works:\nThe pattern Verb て-form (te-form) + も (mo) means \"even if ~\" or \"even though ~.\" It expresses that the outcome will not change regardless of the condition. For い-adjectives (i-adjectives): drop い (i), add くても (kutemo). For nouns/な-adjectives: でも (demo).\n\nExample from this song:\n叩き付けられても (tatakitsukerarete mo) — \"even if beaten down\"\nNo matter how many times the singer is knocked down, they refuse to give up.\n\nMore examples:\n• 雨が降っても行く (ame ga futte mo iku) — \"even if it rains, I'll go\"\n• どんなに辛くても諦めない (donna ni tsurakutemo akiramenai) — \"no matter how painful, I won't give up\"\n• 嫌われても構わない (kirawarete mo kamawanai) — \"I don't care even if I'm hated\""
      },
      "conjugation_path": "叩き付けられる (tatakitsukerareru, \"to be beaten down\") → 叩き付けられて (tatakitsukerarete, te-form) + も (mo) → 叩き付けられても (tatakitsukerarete mo, \"even if beaten down\")"
    },
    {
      "name": "〜わけがない (wake ga nai) — there's no way / impossible",
      "jlpt_reference": "JLPT N3",
      "explanation": {
